{"type": "assistant", "message": {"role": "assistant", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "## Interview synthesis\n\nThree of the eight testers (P3, P6, P8) stopped scanning after a wrong book was added for them. Four themes come up again and again:\n\n- **A wrong book costs trust fast** (P3, P6, P8): all three stopped scanning after a wrong book was added for them.\n- **Glare from glass doors makes scanning unreliable** (P3, P2): Denise's glass door in the afternoon sun.\n- **Testers want to check the list before it is saved** (P1, P4, P7): they would tap through it rather than find out later.\n- **Fixing a miss must take one tap** (P4, P5, P7): nobody wants to retype a title.\n\nTwo quotes carry it:\n\n- **P3 Denise**: “The glass door throws the afternoon sun straight back at the camera. Then my own box has a book on it that isn’t there.”\n- **P8 Owen**: “Two wrong books and I stopped. I don’t have time to audit it.”\n\nI wrote it up in `docs/beta-interview-synthesis.docx` (Summary, What we heard, Themes, Recommendations). The recommendation: show what the scan found and let the steward review it before anything is added, make fixing a missed book one tap, and warn about glare before the photo is taken."}]}, "timestamp": "2026-10-13T08:41:00.000Z", "cwd": "/Users/sam/work/little-shared-library/shelf-scan"}
